  "measurement_note": "Size S is n, the number of nodes. Legal chain tiers 6, 24, and 96 span 16x. Values cycle through six distinct one-digit masks, keeping nontrivial reachable mask combinations in every long suffix. With the digit universe fixed, the accepted postorder merge processes each edge once and scales linearly in S. A correct calibrated alternative rebuilds a digit-mask knapsack independently for every rooted subtree; the chain has Theta(S^2) total subtree membership, so it must fail only scaling.",
